row">Circular value</span><h2>From biological resources to agricultural value.</h2><div class="flow"><div><b>01</b>Organic resources</div><div><b>02</b>BSF bioconversion</div><div><b>03</b>Biological processing</div><div><b>04</b>Bioactivation</div><div><b>05</b>Healthier farms</div><div><b>06</b>Data & green enterprise</div></div></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#8ee2a8">Flagship innovation</span><h2>Meet BioVitalix B+</h2><p class="lead">Next-generation biological plant nutrition technology developed through MarinBio’s proprietary bioactivation approach using Black Soldier Fly-derived biomaterials and beneficial biological components.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/biovitalix">Discover the Science</a></div><div class="card"><span class="pill">Under validation</span><h3 style="margin-top:18px">Designed for the soil–root–microbe relationship.</h3><ul class="check"><li>Supports nutrient bioavailability</li><li>Supports beneficial soil activity</li><li>Promotes rhizosphere development</li><li>Supports regenerative production</li></ul></div></div></section>${quoteBand('your regenerative agriculture priorities')}<script>window.__slides=${JSON.stringify(slides)}</script>`}
function about(){return pageHero('About MarinBio','African science, circular innovation and practical agricultural systems.',images.farm)+`<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Our company</span><h2>Building biological technologies for African agriculture.</h2><p class="lead">MarinBio operates at the intersection of biotechnology, Black Soldier Fly technology, soil regeneration, climate-smart agriculture, controlled-environment production and digital agriculture.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Mission</h3><p>Transform agricultural waste into high-performance biological technologies that regenerate soils, improve productivity and strengthen food security.</p><h3 style="margin-top:25px">Vision</h3><p>Become Africa’s leading biological technology company powering regenerative agriculture through biotechnology, circular bioeconomy, digital agriculture and artificial intelligence.</p></div></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Our model</span><h2>Research → Develop → Validate → Deploy → Monitor → Improve → Scale</h2><div class="grid g3"><div class="card"><h3>Waste is a biological resource</h3><p>Organic materials can become valuable inputs, technologies and enterprises.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Soil is a living system</h3><p>Regeneration requires attention to biological, physical and chemical relationships.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Farmers require evidence</h3><p>MarinBio distinguishes product ambition from verified field and laboratory evidence.</p></div></div></div></section>${quoteBand('a partnership with MarinBio')}`}
function biovitalix(){return pageHero('BioVitalix B+','Next-generation biological plant nutrition technology for regenerative production.',images.soil)+`<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Flagship innovation</span><h2>Designed for the soil–root–microbe relationship.</h2><p class="lead">BioVitalix B+ is developed through MarinBio’s proprietary bioactivation process using Black Soldier Fly-derived biomaterials and beneficial biological components.</p><ul class="check"><li>Designed to support nutrient bioavailability</li><li>Supports beneficial soil biological activity</li><li>Promotes rhizosphere development</li><li>Supports soil regeneration and crop vigour</li><li>Has the potential to reduce dependence on synthetic inputs</li></ul></div><img class="media" src="${images.soil}" alt="Soil and biological plant nutrition"></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Responsible positioning</span><h2>Clear about what BioVitalix is—and is not.</h2><div class="compare"><div class="panel not"><h3>BioVitalix B+ is not</h3><ul class="check"><li>Raw organic waste</li><li>Ordinary compost</li><li>Untreated BSF frass</li><li>A conventional synthetic fertilizer</li><li>A guaranteed crop-disease treatment</li></ul></div><div class="panel is"><h3>BioVitalix B+ is</h3><ul class="check"><li>Bioactivated</li><li>Biologically informed</li><li>Soil-health focused</li><li>Designed for regenerative production</li><li>Supported by application guidance</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#8ee2a8">Evidence before exaggeration</span><h2>Validation remains central.</h2><p class="lead">Product protocols, field observations, soil testing and research partnerships will be published as verified evidence becomes available.</p></div><div class="notice">BioVitalix B+ must not be represented as a registered fungicide, pesticide or guaranteed disease-control product unless formal regulatory evidence is available.</div></div></section>${quoteBand('BioVitalix B+ product, research or distribution requirements')}`}
function solutionsPage(){return pageHero('Agricultural Solutions','Biological, circular and controlled-environment technologies designed around real production needs.',images.greenhouse)+`<section class="section"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Solution portfolio</span><h2>Explore each solution in detail.</h2><div class="grid g3">${cards()}</div></div></section>${quoteBand('a farm system, training programme or advisory assignment')}`}
function solution(slug){const s=solutions[slug];if(!s)return notFound();return pageHero(s.title,s.intro,s.img)+`<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">${s.tag}</span><h2>A solution designed around context—not a generic package.</h2><p class="lead">${s.intro}</p><ul class="check">${s.options.map(x=>`<li>${x}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div><img class="media" src="${s.img}" alt="${s.title}"></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Delivery process</span><div class="grid g4"><div class="card"><h3>1. Assess</h3><p>Review goals, site, scale, resources and operational capacity.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>2. Design</h3><p>Develop a suitable technical scope and implementation plan.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>3. Install or deliver</h3><p>Implement the agreed system, service or training programme.</p></div><div class="card">